# Domain Lexicon (exact terms — no synonyms)

| Use | Not |
|-----|-----|
| Campaign | Game, Adventure, Session |
| Character | Toon, Avatar, PlayerUnit |
| NPC | Mob, Actor, NonPlayer |
| Enemy | Monster, Hostile, Foe |
| Ability | Spell, Power, Skill (unless template defines) |
| Template | Schema, Form, Blueprint |
| Character Sheet | TemplateInstance, CharSheet, StatBlock |
| Item Card | ItemInstance, LootEntry |
| Ability Card | AbilityInstance, SpellInstance |
| Sheet | Instance, FilledForm, Doc (generic filled template doc) |
| Wiki | Lore, Codex (UI label: **Game Reference**) |

# Component filenames (PascalCase.svelte)

- Modals: `[Feature][Action]Modal.svelte` — e.g. `CampaignCreateModal.svelte`
- Overlays: `[Feature]Overlay.svelte` / `[Feature]Drawer.svelte`
- Menus: `[Feature]Menu.svelte`
- Buttons: `[Action]Button.svelte` — e.g. `JoinGameButton.svelte`
- Template editor: `TE_` prefix — e.g. `TE_Canvas.svelte`

# Code style

- **TS/Svelte:** `camelCase` vars/functions; `PascalCase` types/components.
- **Go:** `camelCase` unexported; `PascalCase` exported.
- **API JSON / DB:** `snake_case`.
- **Routes:** kebab-case paths; **Go files:** `snake_case.go`.

Check `$lib/components` before duplicating UI.
